---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import FitDiagnostic from '../../components/FitDiagnostic.astro';
// UTM contract: utm_content=go-receipts
---
<BaseLayout title="We Run the Engine We Install | Buildwise Media" description="See how Buildwise uses the same owned AI engine it installs for service businesses." noindex={true}>
<main><section class="hero"><div class="container hero-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">The Receipts · We are the case study</p><!-- @bwm-exp-slot: hero-headline --><h1 data-bwm-exp-slot="hero-headline">This site runs on the same kind of engine we install.</h1><p class="deck">Our own website and ads are built and operated with our AI engine. People set the aim, and the work gets quality review appropriate to the job.</p><div class="ctas"><!-- @bwm-exp-slot: hero-cta --><a class="cta" href="#diagnostic" data-cta-source="receipts-hero-primary" data-bwm-exp-slot="hero-cta">Get My Free Revenue Leak Map <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a class="cta-ghost" href="/book" data-cta-source="receipts-hero-secondary">See If We're a Fit</a></div><p class="qual mono">For established service businesses with real revenue. Owners looking for a savior bounce off — and that is the right outcome.</p></div>
<!-- @r020:F1 proof: the existing receipts still life grounds the case-study claim in visible working documents -->
<figure><img src="/images/bwm-receipts-still-life-v1.webp" alt="Printed reports and working notes arranged on a dark table" width="640" height="426" loading="eager" decoding="async"/><figcaption class="mono">The work leaves a trail people can inspect.</figcaption></figure></div></section>
<section class="proof"><div class="container"><p class="section-tag">WHY WORK WITH US?</p><h2>Because we are AI engineers.</h2><p class="lede">We understand AI architecture. We do not hand you a prompt and walk away. A dedicated engineering team builds, maintains, and security-engineers an engine the client owns. We test and monitor it as the work changes.</p><div class="cards"><article><span class="tag">AVAILABLE NOW</span><strong>4 HRS → 47 SEC</strong><h3>Lead response</h3><p>This result is already in print on our current pages. It shows the kind of narrow, measured job an engine can improve.</p></article><article><span class="tag">AVAILABLE NOW</span><strong>DAY TO DAY</strong><h3>Client use</h3><p>Clients work with our AI each day. It helps with routine work while people keep control of judgment calls.</p></article><article><span class="tag">AVAILABLE NOW</span><strong>THIS SITE</strong><h3>Our own system</h3><p>The site you are reading was built and is operated this way. Our ads use the same working method.</p></article></div></div></section>
<section class="process"><div class="container"><p class="section-tag">HOW IT REALLY RUNS</p><h2>Automation has gates.</h2><p class="lede">A useful engine knows when to act and when to stop. High-stakes decisions get quality review appropriate to the work. That is not a limit we hide. It is part of sound engineering.</p>
<!-- @r020:F2 proof: a gated loop shows where quality review sits inside the operating system -->
<figure class="loop"><svg viewBox="0 0 800 210" role="img" aria-label="A loop from observe to draft to quality gate to action to measure"><circle cx="92" cy="105" r="48"/><circle cx="250" cy="105" r="48"/><circle class="hot" cx="408" cy="105" r="55"/><circle cx="574" cy="105" r="48"/><circle cx="724" cy="105" r="48"/><path d="M140 105h62m96 0h55m110 0h63m96 0h54"/><text x="64" y="110">OBSERVE</text><text x="231" y="110">DRAFT</text><text x="378" y="101">QUALITY</text><text x="385" y="117">GATE</text><text x="554" y="110">ACT</text><text x="698" y="110">MEASURE</text></svg><figcaption class="mono">The review matches the stakes.</figcaption></figure>
<div class="fiduciary"><span class="mono">THE FIDUCIARY FRAME</span><h2>Your engine should serve your business.</h2><p>We design around your goals, your risk, and your data. You own the delivered code and business assets. Our job is to keep the engine useful, tested, and clear enough to audit.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="close"><div class="container"><p class="section-tag">THE RECEIPT THAT MATTERS</p><h2>Start with one leak you can measure.</h2><p>We will map it before we ask you to build. The first proof should be clear enough for an owner to check.</p><div class="trust"><span>Targets and measurement rules in the work order</span><span>Month-to-month after day 90</span></div></div></section><FitDiagnostic /></main></BaseLayout>
<style>
.hero{padding:clamp(96px,11vw,160px) 0 80px}.hero-grid{display:grid;gap:48px;align-items:center}.hero h1{font-size:clamp(40px,6.5vw,74px);line-height:1;letter-spacing:-.045em}.deck,.lede{font-size:clamp(18px,2vw,22px);line-height:1.6;color:var(--ink-dim);max-width:780px}.ctas{display:flex;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:28px}.qual{font-size:11px;line-height:1.6;color:var(--ink-faint);max-width:650px}figure img{width:100%;display:block}figcaption{font-size:10px;color:var(--ink-faint);margin-top:10px}.proof,.process,.close{padding:clamp(64px,8vw,112px) 0;border-top:1px solid var(--rule)}.proof{background:var(--bg-elev)}h2{font-size:clamp(30px,4.5vw,52px);line-height:1.08;letter-spacing:-.03em;margin:20px 0}.cards{display:grid;gap:1px;background:var(--rule);margin-top:44px}.cards article{background:var(--bg);padding:30px}.cards strong{display:block;color:#F0FF00;font:700 clamp(25px,3vw,38px) 'JetBrains Mono',monospace;margin:22px 0 8px}.cards p,.fiduciary p,.close p{color:var(--ink-dim);font-size:17px;line-height:1.65}.tag{font:700 9px 'JetBrains Mono',monospace;letter-spacing:.12em;color:#050507;background:#F0FF00;padding:5px 7px}.loop{overflow:auto;margin:48px 0}.loop svg{min-width:760px;width:100%}.loop circle{fill:none;stroke:#62626A}.loop .hot{stroke:#F0FF00}.loop path{stroke:#F0FF00}.loop text{fill:#EDEDF0;font:11px 'JetBrains Mono',monospace}.fiduciary{border-left:3px solid #F0FF00;padding:10px 0 10px 30px;max-width:760px}.fiduciary>span{color:#F0FF00;font-size:10px}.trust{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:18px;margin-top:30px}.trust span{border:1px solid var(--rule);padding:16px;color:#F0FF00;font:11px 'JetBrains Mono',monospace}@media(min-width:900px){.hero-grid{grid-template-columns:1.2fr .8fr}.cards{grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr)}}
</style>
